# Boolean fit checks — never printed or sliced, rendered by gate.sh.
# fit-bit: a NOMINAL steel shank (bit_af, no clearance) seated exactly as the
#   bit seats — bottom on the pocket floor — intersected with the production
#   rail solid. Zero facets = the shank clears every pocket face by
#   hex_fit/2 at the production fit. Meaningful, not coincident: hex_fit is
#   0.1, so the clearance is real volume, not a surface kiss.
# fit-bit-ctrl: the same boolean with the shank grown 0.4 across flats —
#   0.2 per side of real interference over the full 12 mm bore. The
#   mandatory negative control: if this ever renders empty, the empty check
#   above is proving nothing.
fit-bit       empty
fit-bit-ctrl  interferes
